## Identified Issues and Limitations

### 1. SPOF (Single Point of Failure)
This infrastructure has a critical SPOF. Since all components (web server, app server, database) are on one machine, if that server fails (hardware failure or OS crash), the entire website becomes unavailable.

### 2. Downtime during Maintenance
Any maintenance task, such as deploying new code or updating the web server configuration, often requires restarting services. Since there is only one server, this process will result in downtime where users cannot access the site.

### 3. Scaling Constraints
This setup is not scalable for high traffic. It can only be scaled **vertically** (adding more RAM/CPU to the same server). If the incoming traffic exceeds the capacity of this single machine, the site will slow down or crash, as there is no way to distribute the load across other servers.
